# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASan test targets.
#
# The NVIDIA driver allocates process-lifetime bookkeeping inside cuInit and
# never frees it. On this box that is a fixed 5,280 bytes in 12 allocations,
# every one of them below cuInit in libcuda.so, and it is reported identically
# on a build with no runner code in the trace at all.
#
# It is suppressed rather than tolerated because the alternative is a leak gate
# that always fails, which is a leak gate nobody reads. `make test-shared-asan`
# exists to catch a refcount that frees early, twice, or never — exactly the
# class of bug the shared-weight records could introduce — and it can only do
# that if a clean run is actually clean.
#
# Scope is deliberately the library, not a wildcard: a leak in runner's own
# frames is still reported even when the allocation happens during a CUDA call.
leak:libcuda.so
